mt7915: fix VoW band setup after add_interface/init_vif split

Upstream openwrt/mt76 (>= 59676919) gained native HW airtime-fairness (VoW)
support and calls mt7915_mcu_set_vow_band(dev, mvif) at the end of
mt7915_add_interface().

MTK's testmode patch (1012-...-add-iBF-eBF-cal-and-cert-commands) splits
mt7915_add_interface() into an mt7915_init_vif() helper plus a thin wrapper,
leaving upstream's trailing call in the wrapper with no mvif local. Move the
call into mt7915_init_vif() instead of re-declaring mvif in the wrapper:

 * testmode's iBF cal/cert path creates a second vif through
   mt7915_init_vif() directly, which now also gets its VoW band configured;
 * the call is skipped when vif init fails, instead of running on a
   half-initialized vif.

Adopted from pesa1234 next-r4.9.1.rss.mtk commit 807e449d22.

--- a/mt7915/main.c
+++ b/mt7915/main.c
@@ -307,6 +307,9 @@ int mt7915_init_vif(struct mt7915_phy *p
 	mt7915_mcu_add_sta(dev, vif, NULL, CONN_STATE_PORT_SECURE, true);
 	rcu_assign_pointer(dev->mt76.wcid[idx], &mvif->sta.wcid);
 
+	if (!is_mt7915(&dev->mt76))
+		mt7915_mcu_set_vow_band(dev, mvif);
+
 	return ret;
 }
 
@@ -329,9 +332,6 @@ static int mt7915_add_interface(struct i
 
 	mutex_unlock(&dev->mt76.mutex);
 
-	if (!is_mt7915(&dev->mt76))
-		mt7915_mcu_set_vow_band(dev, mvif);
-
 	return ret;
 }
 
